WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.134
"What?" Ben gasped.

2
00:00:07.135 --> 00:00:09.708
"That mummy is your uncle?"

3
00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:15.366
Cleo nodded. "My uncle Tut has been missing for a thousand years.

4
00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:17.700
I never thought I'd find him here.

5
00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:20.651
The people must have kidnapped him!"

6
00:00:20.652 --> 00:00:24.530
"People are horrible!" said a vampire.

7
00:00:24.531 --> 00:00:28.055
"Yeah!" agreed the fish monster.

8
00:00:28.056 --> 00:00:33.573
"I think we're supposed to be giving people a chance," Ben reminded everyone.

9
00:00:33.574 --> 00:00:38.413
"Well, people aren't giving monsters a chance," said Mog.

10
00:00:38.414 --> 00:00:44.557
"They're putting mummies on display. This isn't a museum—it's a prison!"

11
00:00:44.558 --> 00:00:47.728
"We're all trapped!" added a goblin.

12
00:00:47.729 --> 00:00:55.250
Ben didn't feel trapped. He could float through the walls and leave at any time.

13
00:00:55.251 --> 00:00:57.440
"Cleo," he said calmly.

14
00:00:57.441 --> 00:01:02.432
"I bet there's a good explanation for why your uncle Tut is here."

15
00:01:02.433 --> 00:01:07.461
Cleo wasn't listening. Instead she was pounding on the display case.

16
00:01:07.462 --> 00:01:14.845
"Uncle Tut!" she cried. "Uncle Tut, can you hear me?"

17
00:01:14.846 --> 00:01:19.336
"Are you sure it's your uncle, Cleo?" Waldo asked.

18
00:01:19.337 --> 00:01:22.605
"You said he's been missing for a thousand years.

19
00:01:22.606 --> 00:01:24.966
How could you even recognize him?"

20
00:01:24.967 --> 00:01:28.655
"A lot of mummies look alike," Gaby chimed in.

21
00:01:28.656 --> 00:01:32.820
"I'm positive!" Cleo insisted.

22
00:01:32.821 --> 00:01:36.682
"My family has a statue of Uncle Tut from when he was king.

23
00:01:36.683 --> 00:01:42.419
And some paintings. That's definitely my uncle!"

24
00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:45.850
Just then Al Normal ran into the room. He

25
00:01:45.851 --> 00:01:52.416
looked frantic. "I heard a scream. Are you monsters okay?" "No."

26
00:01:52.417 --> 00:01:55.167
Mog shook his head. "Someone

27
00:01:55.168 --> 00:02:00.196
is killing monsters and putting them on display. It's not fair!" "What?"

28
00:02:00.197 --> 00:02:03.658
Al Normal shook his head in confusion. "No,

29
00:02:03.659 --> 00:02:06.503
that's not true." "It's

30
00:02:06.504 --> 00:02:10.052
not just monsters," said the fish monster. "I

31
00:02:10.053 --> 00:02:14.116
saw lots of stuffed people in the Early Humans exhibit." Al

32
00:02:14.117 --> 00:02:19.226
Normal sighed. "Monsters, please relax. Those

33
00:02:19.227 --> 00:02:21.384
aren't real people. They're

34
00:02:21.384 --> 00:02:26.960
dummies—life-size models made to look like cave people." "Oh,"

35
00:02:26.961 --> 00:02:31.282
Mog said. "Well, they look pretty real." "Mr.

36
00:02:31.283 --> 00:02:38.481
Normal, are you saying that's not a real mummy?" Waldo asked, pointing at the display. "Of

37
00:02:38.482 --> 00:02:42.633
course it's a genuine mummy," Al Normal said. "All

38
00:02:42.634 --> 00:02:47.042
of our Egyptian displays come from ancient Egypt. That's

39
00:02:47.043 --> 00:02:51.421
the genuine mummy of Tutmosis the Thirteenth." "Uncle

40
00:02:51.422 --> 00:02:54.569
Tut!" Cleo wailed. "I

41
00:02:54.570 --> 00:03:01.198
told you it was my uncle Tut! What have you done to him?" "Young

42
