Cleo looked at him. "That would be so great.

67
00:05:11.378 --> 00:05:13.696
But how can we wake him up?"

68
00:05:13.697 --> 00:05:17.435
"I could throw the case in the fountain," Gaby suggested.

69
00:05:17.436 --> 00:05:19.960
"The cold water might wake him up." "Uh

70
00:05:19.961 --> 00:05:24.814
. . ." Ben glanced uneasily at Dr. Bones. "I

71
00:05:24.815 --> 00:05:29.287
don't think the people would like that," he said. "Maybe

72
00:05:29.288 --> 00:05:33.432
I could float through the case and shake him awake." "Good

73
00:05:33.433 --> 00:05:36.262
idea," Winnie said. "My

74
00:05:36.263 --> 00:05:41.850
spell book is upstairs with my stuff," Waldo said, reaching into his pockets. "But

75
00:05:41.851 --> 00:05:45.607
I have a wand with me. I can try a magic spell." "Oh

76
00:05:45.608 --> 00:05:49.643
no," Ben thought, trying not to groan. By

77
00:05:49.644 --> 00:05:52.079
now Dr. Bones was shouting. "Monster

78
00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:57.660
children! Step away from the displays right now!" "It's

79
00:05:57.661 --> 00:06:02.241
not a display!" Cleo wailed. "It's my uncle!" Waldo

80
